    "reason": "The release note [ev-f445c4712c8b] and the PR [ev-4324f39c9cc6] only say that Argo CD now always requests the `federated:id` scope from Dex. The PR's description is just \"Fixes #17908\". The linked issue [ev-ebb839867b91, ev-da9315ae0d43] describes a symptom: LDAP users logging in through Dex get policy.default but not their policy.csv policies. Its excerpt is cut off, though, and never says which setups were affected or what changes for an operator who does nothing on upgrade. The PR also edits the 2.14→3.0 upgrade guide (docs/operator-manual/upgrading/2.14-3.0.md) [ev-e3cfa368fd32], so it likely has upgrade-relevant effects, perhaps on how users are identified for RBAC. That upgrade-guide section isn't shown, and the PR diff for util/oidc/oidc.go and common/common.go is missing too; both are needed to decide applicability and consequence.",
